From: E200 firmware contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: add an explicit E200 AD9363 dual-RX trial variant

Original source: E200 board port of MicroPhase v0.39 DTS, plus ADI ad9361.c ID table.
Purpose: the vendor ad9364 compatible forces rx2tx2=false even with the DT flag.
Hardware function affected: both receive paths and their CMOS/ADC interface.
Upstream status: E200-specific experimental board variant, not submitted.
Reason local: requires simultaneous dual-RX hardware validation before promotion.
License: GPL-2.0-only. No claim of phase coherence or measured alignment.

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/xilinx/zynq-e200-dual-rx.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/xilinx/zynq-e200-dual-rx.dts
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..47f157d7b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/xilinx/zynq-e200-dual-rx.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/* E200 AD9363 dual-RX trial; RF bandwidth/range remain limited to AD9363. */
+#include "zynq-e200.dts"
+
+&adc0_ad9364 {
+	compatible = "adi,ad9363a";
+	adi,2rx-2tx-mode-enable;
+};
